#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""yabai-layout — snapshot and restore yabai's BSP window layout, frame by frame.

A TILER tool (`tiler/`, installed next to `tiler/learn`), distinct from
`desktop.py`'s `save_layout`/`apply_layout`: those save a named, portable
layout (fractions/roles, replayed through System Events or yabai's own
placement); this one saves the EXACT live BSP tree of one desk — split
ratios, swaps, zooms, floats, focus — so a `yabai --restart-service` (which
rebuilds every tree from scratch and loses all of that) can be undone.

    yabai-layout save    [--file PATH]              # PATH default: see below
    yabai-layout restore [--file PATH] [--wait SEC]  # SEC default: 30
    yabai-layout restore --remap [--file PATH]       # after a login, see below
    yabai-layout verify  [--file PATH]
    yabai-layout place   [--file PATH] [--dry-run]   # after a login, see below
    yabai-layout same-desktops [--file PATH]         # exit 0: no Desktop renumbered

Desktops are saved by monitor (its uuid) and place on it, and translated to
today's numbers before place and restore --remap act: see "Desktops by
monitor" below.

place (used by the Gallery's after-login pass, before restore --remap): puts
every open window back on the Desktop it was on when the snapshot was saved,
terminals and other apps without a home rule included. Saved and open windows
are matched across all Desktops, app by app: by app and title where that pair
is unique on both sides, then the rest in creation order (saved ids, open ids).
A window whose saved Desktop no longer exists (a display not connected now) is
left where it is, as are minimized windows and ones yabai cannot reach.

--remap (used by `gallery home save` / the Gallery's after-login pass): window
ids change at every login, so the saved windows are first matched to the
windows open now, Space by Space -- by app and title where that pair is
unique, then by app in id order. Only a Space whose saved tiled windows all
find a match, with nothing extra tiled there now, is rebuilt; any other Space
is left as it is, and so is one already in the saved shape. Floating windows
are not touched. Which of several windows of one app lands in which slot is
therefore not guaranteed; the shape (splits, sides, ratios) is.

Default snapshot file: ~/.config/yabai/layout-snapshot.json

No scripting addition, ever (SIP stays enabled): never `--load-sa`, and
`yabai -m space --focus`/`--switch` are never called — only window-level
commands, which work on background Spaces without switching to them.

--- How restore rebuilds a Space (empirical yabai 7.1.25 findings) --------

yabai does not persist ad hoc `--toggle float` state across a service
restart (only rule-based manage=off survives), and a saved BSP tree cannot
be replayed as a batch of frames — yabai only exposes structural primitives
(insert direction, warp, ratio). So each Space is rebuilt leaf by leaf:

  1. RECONSTRUCT THE TREE FROM SAVED FRAMES. A genuine BSP node's rect
     always admits a full cut (a vertical or horizontal line with every
     child rect entirely on one side); recurse to a binary tree, deriving
     each node's split ratio from the child frames (see `_ratio_of`).
     "first" = the top/left side, "second" = bottom/right — this is a
     yabai invariant (confirmed empirically: split_child follows screen
     position, not creation order).

  2. REPLAY. `anchor` = the first (top/left-most) leaf; it never moves.
     Every other saved-tiled window is floated up front (removes it from
     whatever tree a restart or --balance left behind). Windows are then
     re-inserted one at a time, pre-order, splitting the anchor's cell:

         yabai -m window <anchor> --insert east|south   # per the cut axis
         yabai -m window <a2>     --toggle float         # unfloat (lands
                                                           # in the FOCUSED
                                                           # space — ignore)
         yabai -m window <a2>     --warp <anchor>         # re-insert here
         yabai -m window <anchor> --ratio abs:<ratio>
         # (the warp consumes the pending insert; a west/west toggle pair
         #  on the anchor clears any leftover once the Space is rebuilt)

     THE KEY FINDING: `--toggle float` always un-floats into the
     currently-FOCUSED Space's tree, never the window's own last Space —
     even if the window was floating ON the target Space already. Doing
     this while focus sits on a different (e.g. the user's live) Space
     transiently splits ONE window there, but `--warp <anchor>` (which
     DOES cross Spaces, and honours the anchor's pending `--insert`
     direction/position) immediately re-homes it correctly, and the
     disturbed Space's tree fully self-heals the instant the interloper
     is warped away. `--warp` itself refuses a still-floating window
     ("the acting window is not managed"), hence the toggle-then-warp
     order. Verified end to end on a live 3-window Space (root + one
     nested split, both axes) with the adjacent, focused Space checked
     clean before and after. `--ratio abs:<r>` is only safe to call on a
     window that is a direct child of the node just created (exactly the
     anchor, right after its warp) — calling it on a window nested two+
     levels inside a pre-existing tree was observed to reshuffle sibling
     order elsewhere in the tree.

  3. Windows present now but absent from the snapshot ("new") and windows
     whose own saved `split_type` was "none" while ≥2 windows share the
     Space ("orphans" — a live yabai quirk: stale/backgrounded windows
     that are `is-floating: false` yet not actually threaded into the
     tree) are floated out during the rebuild and released at the end for
     yabai to place; both are reported, neither gates `verify`. Windows
     with `stack-index > 0` are unsupported: the whole Space is left
     untouched and reported.

Ratio formula: ratio = (first_child_extent + gap/2) / node_extent, where
node_extent is the bounding extent of the node's own children along the
cut axis (window frames already exclude gaps). Verified exact for a
2544px-wide 0.5 vertical split (1268/1268, gap 8): (1268 + 4) / 2544 = 0.5.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path

DEFAULT_FILE = Path.home() / ".config/yabai/layout-snapshot.json"
EPS_MARGIN = 2  # eps for cut-finding = window_gap + EPS_MARGIN, per the spec


class LayoutError(Exception):
    """A Space's saved frames don't admit a clean BSP bisection."""


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# yabai client
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def yabai(*args: str, check: bool = True) -> str:
    """Run `yabai -m <args>`. Returns stripped stdout. Raises RuntimeError
    (with yabai's stderr/stdout) on a non-zero exit unless check=False, in
    which case failures are swallowed and "" is returned — used for
    best-effort commands (toggling a window that may no longer exist,
    clearing an --insert state, re-zooming, etc.)."""
    proc = subprocess.run(["yabai", "-m", *args], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        if check:
            msg = proc.stderr.strip() or proc.stdout.strip() or f"exit {proc.returncode}"
            raise RuntimeError(f"yabai -m {' '.join(args)}: {msg}")
        return ""
    return proc.stdout.strip()


def yabai_json(*args: str):
    out = yabai(*args)
    return json.loads(out) if out else []


def query_windows():
    return web_app_names(yabai_json("query", "--windows"))


# A web app added to the Dock from Safari runs in Safari's generic Web App
# process, and yabai often names its windows "Web App". bin/gallery saves them
# under the name macOS gives the app (lsappinfo); so do the snapshots here, or
# a saved Outlook would never match the live window.
_WEB_APP_NAMES: dict = {}


def web_app_names(windows):
    for w in windows if isinstance(windows, list) else []:
        if not isinstance(w, dict) or w.get("app") != "Web App" or not isinstance(w.get("pid"), int):
            continue
        pid = w["pid"]
        if pid not in _WEB_APP_NAMES:
            _WEB_APP_NAMES[pid] = None
            try:
                asn = subprocess.run(["lsappinfo", "find", f"pid={pid}"], capture_output=True,
                                     text=True, timeout=5).stdout.strip()
                out = subprocess.run(["lsappinfo", "info", "-only", "name", asn], capture_output=True,
                                     text=True, timeout=5).stdout if asn else ""
                m = re.match(r'\s*"([^"]+)"', out)
                _WEB_APP_NAMES[pid] = m.group(1) if m else None
            except Exception:
                pass
        w["app"] = _WEB_APP_NAMES[pid] or w["app"]
    return windows


def query_spaces():
    return yabai_json("query", "--spaces")


def query_window_by_id(win_id: int):
    out = yabai("query", "--windows", "--window", str(win_id), check=False)
    return json.loads(out) if out else None


def query_displays():
    return yabai_json("query", "--displays")


def config_int(key: str, default: int) -> int:
    out = yabai("config", key, check=False)
    try:
        return int(float(out))
    except ValueError:
        return default


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# save
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def cmd_save(args) -> int:
    path = Path(args.file).expanduser()

    windows_before = query_windows()
    zoom_state = {w["id"]: (w["has-fullscreen-zoom"], w["has-parent-zoom"]) for w in windows_before}

    # Un-zoom every zoomed window BEFORE recording frames: a zoomed window's
    # frame hides its real tile, and it must be un-zoomed to read that frame.
    for w in windows_before:
        if w["has-fullscreen-zoom"]:
            yabai("window", str(w["id"]), "--toggle", "zoom-fullscreen", check=False)
        if w["has-parent-zoom"]:
            yabai("window", str(w["id"]), "--toggle", "zoom-parent", check=False)
    if any(zoom_state.values()):
        time.sleep(0.2)

    windows = query_windows()
    spaces = query_spaces()
    displays = query_displays()
    # NB: a window's own "space" field (query --windows) is the Space's
    # mission-control INDEX, not its internal "id" — confirmed empirically
    # (a Space with id=12/index=8 shows "space": 8 on its windows). Index is
    # therefore the key used everywhere windows are matched to a Space;
    # "id" is carried along as informational metadata only.
    space_by_index = {s["index"]: s for s in spaces}

    gap = config_int("window_gap", 8)
    padding = {
        "top": config_int("top_padding", 8),
        "bottom": config_int("bottom_padding", 8),
        "left": config_int("left_padding", 8),
        "right": config_int("right_padding", 8),
    }

    focused_window = None
    where = desktop_positions(displays)
    spaces_out: dict[str, dict] = {}
    for s in spaces:
        uuid, pos = where.get(s["index"], (None, None))
        spaces_out[str(s["index"])] = {
            "space_id": s["id"],
            "space_index": s["index"],
            "display": s["display"],
            "display_uuid": uuid,
            "display_space": pos,
            "type": s["type"],
            "windows": [],
        }

    for w in windows:
        if w.get("has-focus"):
            focused_window = w["id"]
        fz, pz = zoom_state.get(w["id"], (False, False))
        sp = space_by_index.get(w["space"], {})
        uuid, pos = where.get(w["space"], (None, None))
        rec = {
            "id": w["id"],
            "app": w["app"],
            "title": w["title"],
            "display": w["display"],
            "display_uuid": uuid,
            "display_space": pos,
            "space_id": sp.get("id"),
            "space_index": w["space"],
            "frame": w["frame"],
            "is_floating": w["is-floating"],
            "is_visible": w["is-visible"],
            "is_minimized": w["is-minimized"],
            "has_fullscreen_zoom": fz,
            "has_parent_zoom": pz,
            "stack_index": w["stack-index"],
            # Auxiliary, yabai-internal: used only by restore to filter out
            # "orphan" windows (is-floating false but not actually threaded
            # into the Space's tree) before bisecting the saved frames.
            "split_type": w["split-type"],
            "split_child": w["split-child"],
        }
        key = str(w["space"])
        spaces_out.setdefault(key, {
            "space_id": sp.get("id"), "space_index": w["space"],
            "display": w["display"], "display_uuid": uuid, "display_space": pos,
            "type": "bsp", "windows": [],
        })
        spaces_out[key]["windows"].append(rec)

    snapshot = {
        "version": 1,
        "created": datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec="seconds"),
        "config": {"window_gap": gap, "padding": padding},
        "displays": [{"id": d["id"], "uuid": d.get("uuid"), "index": d["index"],
                      "spaces": d.get("spaces"), "frame": d["frame"]} for d in displays],
        "focused_window": focused_window,
        "spaces": spaces_out,
    }

    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    path.write_text(json.dumps(snapshot, indent=2) + "\n")
    # Put back the zoom undone above: saving must not change the desktop.
    for wid, (fz, pz) in zoom_state.items():
        if fz:
            yabai("window", str(wid), "--toggle", "zoom-fullscreen", check=False)
        if pz:
            yabai("window", str(wid), "--toggle", "zoom-parent", check=False)
    n_windows = sum(len(s["windows"]) for s in spaces_out.values())
    print(f"[yabai-layout] saved {n_windows} windows across {len(spaces_out)} spaces -> {path}")
    return 0


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# geometry / bisection
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def _l(w):
    return w["frame"]["x"]


def _r(w):
    return w["frame"]["x"] + w["frame"]["w"]


def _t(w):
    return w["frame"]["y"]


def _b(w):
    return w["frame"]["y"] + w["frame"]["h"]


def _find_cut(rects, axis, eps):
    """A clean full cut along `axis` ('x': vertical line, left/right;
    'y': horizontal line, top/bottom). Candidates are each rect's
    trailing edge; returns (first_side, second_side) or None."""
    lo, hi = (_l, _r) if axis == "x" else (_t, _b)
    candidates = sorted({hi(r) for r in rects})
    for c in candidates[:-1]:
        first = [r for r in rects if hi(r) <= c + eps]
        second = [r for r in rects if lo(r) >= c - eps]
        if not first or not second:
            continue
        if len(first) + len(second) != len(rects):
            continue
        if set(id(r) for r in first) & set(id(r) for r in second):
            continue
        return first, second
    return None


def _ratio_of(first, whole, axis, gap):
    if axis == "x":
        node_extent = max(_r(w) for w in whole) - min(_l(w) for w in whole)
        first_extent = max(_r(w) for w in first) - min(_l(w) for w in first)
    else:
        node_extent = max(_b(w) for w in whole) - min(_t(w) for w in whole)
        first_extent = max(_b(w) for w in first) - min(_t(w) for w in first)
    if node_extent <= 0:
        return 0.5
    return (first_extent + gap / 2.0) / node_extent


def bisect_tree(rects, gap, eps):
    """Recursively reconstruct the BSP tree from a set of saved window
    frames. Raises LayoutError if some node's rect doesn't admit a clean
    full cut (not a genuine BSP partition — caller should have already
    filtered out orphans/stacks/floats/missing windows)."""
    if len(rects) == 1:
        return {"leaf": rects[0]}
    cut = _find_cut(rects, "x", eps)
    axis = "x"
    if cut is None:
        cut = _find_cut(rects, "y", eps)
        axis = "y"
    if cut is None:
        names = ", ".join(f'{w["app"]}#{w["id"]}' for w in rects)
        raise LayoutError(f"no clean bisection for {len(rects)} windows ({names})")
    first, second = cut
    ratio = _ratio_of(first, rects, axis, gap)
    return {
        "axis": axis,
        "ratio": ratio,
        "first": bisect_tree(first, gap, eps),
        "second": bisect_tree(second, gap, eps),
    }


def first_leaf(node):
    while "leaf" not in node:
        node = node["first"]
    return node["leaf"]


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# restore
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def wait_for_yabai(timeout: float, saved_ids: set[int]) -> bool:
    """Poll until yabai answers --query --windows, at least one saved window
    id shows up managed, and the window count holds still across two
    consecutive polls — right after a restart yabai is still enumerating
    windows, and rebuilding on a partial list would misplace the rest."""
    deadline = time.time() + timeout
    last_count = None
    while time.time() < deadline:
        try:
            windows = query_windows()
        except Exception:
            windows = None
        if windows is not None:
            if not saved_ids or any(w["id"] in saved_ids for w in windows):
                if last_count == len(windows):
                    return True
                last_count = len(windows)
        time.sleep(0.5)
    # One last try, in case saved_ids is empty or nothing ever matched.
    try:
        query_windows()
        return True
    except Exception:
        return False


def _classify(saved_windows):
    """Split a Space's saved window list into: tiled (is_floating False,
    is_minimized False), floats, and (within tiled) stacked vs. flat."""
    tiled = [w for w in saved_windows if not w["is_floating"] and not w["is_minimized"]]
    floats = [w for w in saved_windows if w["is_floating"] and not w["is_minimized"]]
    stacked = [w for w in tiled if w.get("stack_index", 0) > 0]
    flat = [w for w in tiled if w.get("stack_index", 0) == 0]
    if len(flat) > 1:
        clean = [w for w in flat if w.get("split_type") != "none"]
        orphans = [w for w in flat if w.get("split_type") == "none"]
    else:
        clean = flat
        orphans = []
    return clean, orphans, stacked, floats


def _float(win_id: int):
    yabai("window", str(win_id), "--toggle", "float", check=False)


def _unfloat_here(win_id: int):
    yabai("window", str(win_id), "--toggle", "float", check=False)


# How long released windows are watched for wandering off their Desktop.
RELEASE_SETTLE_S = 1.5


def _release_on(win_ids, space_index):
    """Un-float win_ids and make sure they stay on space_index. Un-floating a
    window on a Desktop that is not in view tiles it into the Desktop that is
    (seen after a restart: Signal and Telegram from Desktop 10 left on
    Desktop 7), and yabai does it a moment later, not at once -- so the
    windows are watched for a while and any that wandered is sent back."""
    win_ids = list(win_ids)
    for wid in win_ids:
        _unfloat_here(wid)
    if not win_ids or not isinstance(space_index, int):
        return
    deadline = time.monotonic() + RELEASE_SETTLE_S
    while True:
        for wid in win_ids:
            w = query_window_by_id(wid)
            if w and w.get("space") != space_index:
                yabai("window", str(wid), "--space", str(space_index), check=False)
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            return
        time.sleep(0.25)


# How long the anchor gets to fill the Desktop once the others are floated:
# on a Desktop not in view yabai applies the new frame late, and a check
# made too soon took that for a window wedged in the tree.
ANCHOR_SETTLE_S = 2.0


def _anchor_expanded(anchor_id: int, exp_w: float, exp_h: float, eps: float) -> bool:
    deadline = time.monotonic() + ANCHOR_SETTLE_S
    while True:
        a = query_window_by_id(anchor_id)
        if a:
            f = a["frame"]
            if abs(f["w"] - exp_w) <= eps and abs(f["h"] - exp_h) <= eps:
                return True
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            return False
        time.sleep(0.15)


def _placed(win_id: int, anchor_id: int, axis: str) -> bool:
    """True if win_id is tiled on anchor_id's Space, directly east (axis x)
    or south (axis y) of it -- where an insert east|south puts it."""
    w, a = query_window_by_id(win_id), query_window_by_id(anchor_id)
    if not w or not a or w.get("space") != a.get("space") or w.get("is-floating"):
        return False
    wf, af = w["frame"], a["frame"]
    eps = 2 * EPS_MARGIN + 8
    if axis == "x":
        return abs(wf["x"] - (af["x"] + af["w"])) <= eps and abs(wf["y"] - af["y"]) <= eps
    return abs(wf["y"] - (af["y"] + af["h"])) <= eps and abs(wf["x"] - af["x"]) <= eps


def _build(node, anchor_id, gap):
    """Pre-order replay: split anchor_id's current cell to place the
    "second" side, recurse into both sides. See module docstring for the
    empirical basis of this exact command sequence."""
    if "leaf" in node:
        return
    axis = node["axis"]
    direction = "east" if axis == "x" else "south"
    c1, c2 = node["first"], node["second"]
    a2 = first_leaf(c2)["id"]

    yabai("window", str(anchor_id), "--insert", direction, check=False)
    _unfloat_here(a2)
    time.sleep(0.15)
    # On the Space in view the un-float itself honours the anchor's pending
    # insert and puts a2 in place; warping it then would move it to the
    # other side. Only a window that landed elsewhere (another Space, the
    # case after a restart with focus away) is warped home.
    if not _placed(a2, anchor_id, axis):
        yabai("window", str(a2), "--warp", str(anchor_id), check=False)
        time.sleep(0.15)
    yabai("window", str(anchor_id), "--ratio", f"abs:{node['ratio']:.4f}", check=False)
    # No "clear" toggle here: the warp consumes the pending insert, and
    # `--insert` is a toggle, so re-issuing the direction would re-arm it
    # (seen live as yabai's red insert-feedback overlay left on the last
    # anchor, and every new window on that Space landing there). Any
    # leftover is cleared once per Space by _clear_insert.

    _build(c1, anchor_id, gap)
    _build(c2, a2, gap)


def _clear_insert(win_id: int):
    """Leave no pending --insert anywhere. yabai keeps at most one pending
    insert, and --insert toggles: setting a direction this tool never uses
    (west) on win_id supersedes whatever was pending, and setting it again
    undoes it -- deterministic regardless of prior state."""
    yabai("window", str(win_id), "--insert", "west", check=False)
    yabai("window", str(win_id), "--insert", "west", check=False)


def restore_space(space_snap, live_by_id, gap, eps, summary: list[str]):
    space_index = space_snap.get("space_index")
    saved = space_snap["windows"]
    clean, orphans, stacked, floats = _classify(saved)

    if stacked:
        names = ", ".join(f'{w["app"]}#{w["id"]}' for w in stacked)
        summary.append(f"space {space_index}: stacked windows unsupported ({names}) — left untouched")
        return

    present = {}
    missing = []
    for w in clean:
        if w["id"] in live_by_id:
            present[w["id"]] = w
        else:
            missing.append(w)

    live_here = [w for w in live_by_id.values() if w["space"] == space_snap["space_index"]]
    saved_clean_ids = {w["id"] for w in clean}
    saved_orphan_ids = {w["id"] for w in orphans}
    saved_float_ids = {w["id"] for w in floats}
    new_ids = set()
    for lw in live_here:
        if lw["id"] in saved_clean_ids or lw["id"] in saved_orphan_ids or lw["id"] in saved_float_ids:
            continue
        if lw["is-floating"] or lw["is-minimized"]:
            continue
        new_ids.add(lw["id"])

    # Float every present tiled/orphan/new window on this space except the
    # anchor, so the rebuild starts from a single tiled leaf.
    anchor_id = None
    if len(present) == 1:
        anchor_id = next(iter(present))
    elif len(present) >= 2:
        try:
            tree = bisect_tree(list(present.values()), gap, eps)
        except LayoutError as e:
            summary.append(f"space {space_index}: {e} — left untouched")
            return
        anchor_id = first_leaf(tree)["id"]

    orphan_ids_present = [w["id"] for w in orphans if w["id"] in live_by_id]
    movable_ids = [wid for wid in list(present) + orphan_ids_present + list(new_ids) if wid != anchor_id]

    # A window with no accessibility reference (a stale/"ghost" yabai record:
    # is-floating false, can-move false, split-type "none", the owning
    # app/window already gone — observed to survive even a full
    # `--restart-service`) cannot be floated or warped. If the anchor itself
    # is one, nothing on this Space is commandable — bail immediately.
    if anchor_id is not None and not live_by_id.get(anchor_id, {}).get("has-ax-reference", True):
        summary.append(f"space {space_index}: anchor window has no accessibility reference "
                        f"({live_by_id[anchor_id]['app']}#{anchor_id}) — left untouched")
        return

    for wid in movable_ids:
        _float(wid)
    time.sleep(0.1)

    # A ghost elsewhere in the Space doesn't always block the rebuild — an
    # orphan (split_type "none") can be either truly detached from the tree
    # (harmless to leave in place) or still occupying a real slot (blocks
    # the anchor from reclaiming that space), and there is no way to tell
    # apart from a window's own fields (observed both cases with identical
    # fields). So check empirically: after floating everything else, the
    # anchor should have expanded to the full bounding box of the saved
    # tiled set. If a ghost is still wedged in the tree, it won't have.
    if len(present) >= 2:
        exp_w = max(_r(w) for w in present.values()) - min(_l(w) for w in present.values())
        exp_h = max(_b(w) for w in present.values()) - min(_t(w) for w in present.values())
        if not _anchor_expanded(anchor_id, exp_w, exp_h, eps):
            _release_on(movable_ids, space_index)
            ghost_names = ", ".join(
                f'{live_by_id[w]["app"]}#{w}' for w in orphan_ids_present + list(new_ids)
                if w in live_by_id and not live_by_id[w].get("has-ax-reference", True)
            )
            extra = f" (likely: {ghost_names})" if ghost_names else ""
            summary.append(f"space {space_index}: an immovable window still occupies a tree "
                            f"slot{extra} — could not fully evacuate, left as close to original "
                            f"as possible (not gated)")
            return
        _build(tree, anchor_id, gap)
        _clear_insert(anchor_id)

    # Release orphans and new windows for yabai to place; report them.
    _release_on(orphan_ids_present + list(new_ids), space_index)

    restored = len(present)
    parts = [f"{restored} restored"]
    if missing:
        parts.append(f"{len(missing)} missing")
    if orphan_ids_present:
        parts.append(f"{len(orphan_ids_present)} orphan (unsupported, released)")
    if new_ids:
        parts.append(f"{len(new_ids)} new (released)")
    summary.append(f"space {space_index}: " + ", ".join(parts))


def restore_floats(snapshot, live_by_id, summary: list[str]):
    n = 0
    for space in snapshot["spaces"].values():
        for w in space["windows"]:
            if not w["is_floating"] or w["is_minimized"]:
                continue
            if w["id"] not in live_by_id:
                continue
            lw = live_by_id[w["id"]]
            if not lw["is-floating"]:
                yabai("window", str(w["id"]), "--toggle", "float", check=False)
            f = w["frame"]
            yabai("window", str(w["id"]), "--move", f"abs:{f['x']:.0f}:{f['y']:.0f}", check=False)
            yabai("window", str(w["id"]), "--resize", f"abs:{f['w']:.0f}:{f['h']:.0f}", check=False)
            n += 1
    if n:
        summary.append(f"floats: {n} repositioned")


def rezoom(snapshot, live_by_id, summary: list[str]):
    n = 0
    for space in snapshot["spaces"].values():
        for w in space["windows"]:
            if w["id"] not in live_by_id:
                continue
            if w.get("has_fullscreen_zoom"):
                yabai("window", str(w["id"]), "--toggle", "zoom-fullscreen", check=False)
                n += 1
            if w.get("has_parent_zoom"):
                yabai("window", str(w["id"]), "--toggle", "zoom-parent", check=False)
                n += 1
    if n:
        summary.append(f"zoom: {n} windows re-zoomed")


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Desktops by monitor
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#
# yabai numbers the Desktops of all displays in one sequence (1-9 on the main
# display, 10-18 on the next), and "display 2" only means the second in its
# order. Both shift: a Desktop added or removed on one display renumbers those
# after it, and another main display or a monitor plugged in elsewhere swaps
# the order. So a snapshot also notes each Desktop's monitor by its permanent
# uuid and its place on that monitor (display_uuid, display_space), and is
# translated to today's numbers before anything is moved. A snapshot from
# before this (no uuids) is used as saved.

def desktop_positions(displays):
    """{global Desktop index: (display uuid, 1-based place on that display)}."""
    out = {}
    for d in displays:
        for pos, index in enumerate(d.get("spaces") or [], start=1):
            out[index] = (d.get("uuid"), pos)
    return out


def translate_snapshot(snapshot, live_displays):
    """Return (snapshot with every Desktop renumbered for the displays
    connected now, notes). A Desktop whose monitor is not connected, or that
    no longer exists on it, is dropped (its windows stay where they are).
    Pure: no yabai calls."""
    spaces = snapshot.get("spaces") or {}
    if not any(sp.get("display_uuid") for sp in spaces.values()):
        return snapshot, []
    live = {d.get("uuid"): d for d in live_displays if d.get("uuid")}
    out = dict(snapshot)
    out["spaces"] = {}
    notes = []
    for key, sp in sorted(spaces.items(), key=lambda kv: kv[1].get("space_index") or 0):
        uuid, pos = sp.get("display_uuid"), sp.get("display_space")
        d = live.get(uuid)
        has_windows = bool(sp.get("windows"))
        if d is None:
            if has_windows:
                notes.append(f"Desktop {sp.get('space_index')}: its display is not connected -- left")
            continue
        here = d.get("spaces") or []
        if not isinstance(pos, int) or pos > len(here):
            if has_windows:
                notes.append(f"Desktop {sp.get('space_index')}: display {d.get('index')} has no Desktop {pos} now -- left")
            continue
        index, display = here[pos - 1], d.get("index")
        if index != sp.get("space_index") and has_windows:
            notes.append(f"Desktop {sp.get('space_index')} is Desktop {index} now (same monitor, same place)")
        new = dict(sp, space_index=index, display=display)
        new["windows"] = [dict(w, space_index=index, display=display) for w in sp.get("windows") or []]
        out["spaces"][str(index)] = new
    return out, notes


def desktops_unchanged(snapshot, live_displays) -> bool:
    """True if every saved Desktop with windows has the same number now."""
    moved, notes = translate_snapshot(snapshot, live_displays)
    if notes:
        return False
    before = {k for k, sp in (snapshot.get("spaces") or {}).items() if sp.get("windows")}
    after = {k for k, sp in moved.get("spaces", {}).items() if sp.get("windows")}
    return before == after


def cmd_same_desktops(args) -> int:
    path = Path(args.file).expanduser()
    if not path.exists():
        return 0
    try:
        snapshot = json.loads(path.read_text())
    except Exception:
        return 0
    return 0 if desktops_unchanged(snapshot, query_displays()) else 1


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# remap (ids change at every login)
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def _tiled_live(windows, space_index):
    return [w for w in windows
            if w["space"] == space_index and not w["is-floating"] and not w["is-minimized"]
            and w.get("has-ax-reference", True) and w.get("stack-index", 0) == 0]


def remap_snapshot(snapshot, live_windows):
    """Return (snapshot with each restorable Space's saved ids replaced by the
    matching live ids, notes). Spaces that cannot be matched completely are
    dropped from the returned snapshot (so restore leaves them alone), as
    are floating and minimized windows. Pure: no yabai calls."""
    out = dict(snapshot)
    out["spaces"] = {}
    out["focused_window"] = None
    notes = []
    for key, space in snapshot["spaces"].items():
        index = space.get("space_index")
        clean, orphans, stacked, _floats = _classify(space["windows"])
        if not clean:
            continue
        if stacked:
            notes.append(f"space {index}: stacked windows unsupported -- left as it is")
            continue
        live = _tiled_live(live_windows, index)
        if len(live) != len(clean):
            notes.append(f"space {index}: {len(clean)} tiled windows saved, {len(live)} open now -- left as it is")
            continue
        unmatched = sorted(live, key=lambda w: w["id"])
        mapping = {}
        # 1. app and title, where that pair is unique on both sides
        def pairs(ws, app_key, title_key):
            seen = {}
            for w in ws:
                seen.setdefault((w[app_key], w[title_key]), []).append(w)
            return seen
        saved_pairs = pairs(clean, "app", "title")
        live_pairs = pairs(unmatched, "app", "title")
        for pair, ws in saved_pairs.items():
            if len(ws) == 1 and len(live_pairs.get(pair, [])) == 1:
                lw = live_pairs[pair][0]
                mapping[ws[0]["id"]] = lw["id"]
                unmatched.remove(lw)
        # 2. app alone, saved windows top-left first, live ones in id order
        rest = sorted((w for w in clean if w["id"] not in mapping),
                      key=lambda w: (w["frame"]["y"], w["frame"]["x"]))
        ok = True
        for w in rest:
            lw = next((x for x in unmatched if x["app"] == w["app"]), None)
            if lw is None:
                ok = False
                break
            mapping[w["id"]] = lw["id"]
            unmatched.remove(lw)
        if not ok or unmatched:
            notes.append(f"space {index}: the open windows are not the saved apps -- left as it is")
            continue
        new_space = dict(space)
        new_space["windows"] = [dict(w, id=mapping[w["id"]]) for w in clean]
        out["spaces"][key] = new_space
    return out, notes


def in_shape(space_snap, live_by_id, eps) -> bool:
    """True if every saved tiled window already sits on its saved frame."""
    for w in space_snap["windows"]:
        lw = live_by_id.get(w["id"])
        if lw is None:
            return False
        sf, lf = w["frame"], lw["frame"]
        if max(abs(sf["x"] - lf["x"]), abs(sf["y"] - lf["y"]),
               abs(sf["w"] - lf["w"]), abs(sf["h"] - lf["h"])) > eps:
            return False
    return True


def visible_spaces() -> set:
    return {s["index"] for s in query_spaces() if s.get("is-visible")}


def return_strays(origin, live_windows) -> int:
    """Send every window whose Desktop differs from origin (id -> space)
    back there; the number sent back."""
    n = 0
    for w in live_windows:
        was = origin.get(w["id"])
        if isinstance(was, int) and w.get("space") != was:
            yabai("window", str(w["id"]), "--space", str(was), check=False)
            n += 1
    return n


def cmd_restore(args) -> int:
    path = Path(args.file).expanduser()
    if not path.exists():
        print(f"[yabai-layout] no snapshot at {path}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    snapshot = json.loads(path.read_text())

    summary: list[str] = []
    if args.remap:
        # (place, which runs first, reports what moved or was left)
        snapshot, _ = translate_snapshot(snapshot, query_displays())
        snapshot, notes = remap_snapshot(snapshot, query_windows())
        summary.extend(notes)
        saved_ids = set()
    else:
        saved_ids = {w["id"] for space in snapshot["spaces"].values() for w in space["windows"]}
    if not wait_for_yabai(args.wait, saved_ids):
        print(f"[yabai-layout] yabai did not answer within {args.wait}s", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1

    gap = snapshot["config"]["window_gap"]
    eps = gap + EPS_MARGIN

    # Restore changes shapes, never a window's Desktop; where each window is
    # now, to send back any that yabai moved to the Desktop in view.
    origin = {w["id"]: w["space"] for w in query_windows()}

    # Only the Desktops in view: yabai does not lay out a Desktop that is not
    # (its windows keep stale frames, an un-floated window lands on the one
    # in view), so a rebuild there floats and un-floats windows into a broken
    # tree instead. Those are left as they are; the tree guard tidies a
    # Desktop when it comes into view.
    in_view = visible_spaces()

    for space in sorted(snapshot["spaces"].values(), key=lambda s: (s["space_index"] or 0)):
        if space.get("space_index") not in in_view:
            summary.append(f"space {space.get('space_index')}: not in view -- left as it is")
            continue
        live_by_id = {w["id"]: w for w in query_windows()}
        if args.remap and in_shape(space, live_by_id, eps):
            summary.append(f"space {space['space_index']}: already in the saved shape")
            continue
        restore_space(space, live_by_id, gap, eps, summary)

    time.sleep(RELEASE_SETTLE_S)
    strays = return_strays(origin, query_windows())
    if strays:
        summary.append(f"sent back to their Desktops: {strays}")

    live_by_id = {w["id"]: w for w in query_windows()}
    restore_floats(snapshot, live_by_id, summary)
    live_by_id = {w["id"]: w for w in query_windows()}
    rezoom(snapshot, live_by_id, summary)

    focused = snapshot.get("focused_window")
    if focused is not None:
        yabai("window", str(focused), "--focus", check=False)

    print("[yabai-layout] restore summary:")
    for line in summary:
        print(f"  {line}")
    return 0


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# place
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def plan_placement(snapshot, live_windows, live_spaces):
    """Return (moves, notes): moves is a list of (live id, app, saved Space
    index) for each open window that sits on another Desktop than its matched
    saved window did. Pure: no yabai calls."""
    saved_by_app: dict[str, list] = {}
    for space in snapshot.get("spaces", {}).values():
        for w in space.get("windows", []):
            if w.get("is_minimized") or not w.get("app"):
                continue
            saved_by_app.setdefault(w["app"], []).append(w)
    live_by_app: dict[str, list] = {}
    for w in live_windows:
        if w.get("is-minimized") or not w.get("has-ax-reference", True) or not w.get("app"):
            continue
        live_by_app.setdefault(w["app"], []).append(w)
    displays_now = {s.get("display") for s in live_spaces}
    spaces_now = {s["index"]: s for s in live_spaces}

    moves, notes = [], []
    for app, live in sorted(live_by_app.items()):
        saved = saved_by_app.get(app)
        if not saved:
            continue
        saved = sorted(saved, key=lambda w: w["id"])
        live = sorted(live, key=lambda w: w["id"])
        pairs = []
        # 1. app and title, where that pair is unique on both sides
        def by_title(ws):
            seen: dict[str, list] = {}
            for w in ws:
                seen.setdefault(w.get("title") or "", []).append(w)
            return seen
        saved_t, live_t = by_title(saved), by_title(live)
        for title, ws in saved_t.items():
            if title and len(ws) == 1 and len(live_t.get(title, [])) == 1:
                pairs.append((live_t[title][0], ws[0]))
        done_saved = {id(sw) for _, sw in pairs}
        done_live = {lw["id"] for lw, _ in pairs}
        # 2. the rest in creation order on both sides
        rest_saved = [w for w in saved if id(w) not in done_saved]
        rest_live = [w for w in live if w["id"] not in done_live]
        pairs.extend(zip(rest_live, rest_saved))
        for lw, sw in pairs:
            target = sw.get("space_index")
            if not isinstance(target, int) or lw.get("space") == target:
                continue
            here = spaces_now.get(target)
            saved_display = sw.get("display")
            if here is None or (saved_display is not None and saved_display not in displays_now):
                notes.append(f"{app}#{lw['id']}: saved on Desktop {target}, which is not here now -- left")
                continue
            moves.append((lw["id"], app, target))
    return moves, notes


def cmd_place(args) -> int:
    path = Path(args.file).expanduser()
    if not path.exists():
        print(f"[yabai-layout] no snapshot at {path}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    snapshot, moved = translate_snapshot(json.loads(path.read_text()), query_displays())
    moves, notes = plan_placement(snapshot, query_windows(), query_spaces())
    notes = moved + notes
    placed = 0
    for wid, app, target in moves:
        if args.dry_run:
            notes.append(f"{app}#{wid}: would move to Desktop {target}")
            continue
        try:
            yabai("window", str(wid), "--space", str(target))
            placed += 1
        except RuntimeError as exc:
            notes.append(f"{app}#{wid}: could not move to Desktop {target} ({exc})")
    print(f"[yabai-layout] placed {placed} of {len(moves)} windows on their saved Desktops")
    for line in notes:
        print(f"  {line}")
    return 0


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# verify
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def cmd_verify(args) -> int:
    path = Path(args.file).expanduser()
    if not path.exists():
        print(f"[yabai-layout] no snapshot at {path}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    snapshot = json.loads(path.read_text())
    live_by_id = {w["id"]: w for w in query_windows()}

    max_delta = 0.0
    gating_ok = True
    for space in sorted(snapshot["spaces"].values(), key=lambda s: (s["space_index"] or 0)):
        clean, orphans, stacked, floats = _classify(space["windows"])
        gating_ids = {w["id"] for w in clean}
        unsupported_ids = {w["id"] for w in orphans} | {w["id"] for w in stacked}
        for w in space["windows"]:
            if w["id"] not in live_by_id:
                continue
            if w["is_floating"] or w["is_minimized"]:
                continue
            lw = live_by_id[w["id"]]
            sf, lf = w["frame"], lw["frame"]
            d_left = abs(sf["x"] - lf["x"])
            d_top = abs(sf["y"] - lf["y"])
            d_right = abs((sf["x"] + sf["w"]) - (lf["x"] + lf["w"]))
            d_bottom = abs((sf["y"] + sf["h"]) - (lf["y"] + lf["h"]))
            delta = max(d_left, d_top, d_right, d_bottom)
            tag = ""
            if w["id"] in unsupported_ids:
                tag = " (unsupported, not gated)"
            else:
                max_delta = max(max_delta, delta)
                if w["id"] in gating_ids and delta > 2:
                    gating_ok = False
            print(f"  space {space['space_index']} {w['app']}#{w['id']}: "
                  f"delta L{d_left:.1f} T{d_top:.1f} R{d_right:.1f} B{d_bottom:.1f} "
                  f"(max {delta:.1f}px){tag}")

    print(f"[yabai-layout] max delta (gating windows): {max_delta:.1f}px — "
          f"{'PASS' if gating_ok else 'FAIL'}")
    return 0 if gating_ok else 1


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# main
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

def main() -> int:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="yabai-layout", description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    sub = ap.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)

    p_save = sub.add_parser("save", help="snapshot the current yabai layout")
    p_save.add_argument("--file", default=str(DEFAULT_FILE))

    p_restore = sub.add_parser("restore", help="replay a saved yabai layout")
    p_restore.add_argument("--file", default=str(DEFAULT_FILE))
    p_restore.add_argument("--wait", type=float, default=30.0)
    p_restore.add_argument("--remap", action="store_true",
                           help="match saved windows to the open ones by app (after a login)")

    p_verify = sub.add_parser("verify", help="compare live frames to a saved snapshot")
    p_verify.add_argument("--file", default=str(DEFAULT_FILE))

    p_place = sub.add_parser("place", help="move open windows to their saved Desktops (after a login)")
    p_place.add_argument("--file", default=str(DEFAULT_FILE))
    p_place.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")

    p_same = sub.add_parser("same-desktops",
                            help="exit 0 if every saved Desktop has the same number now")
    p_same.add_argument("--file", default=str(DEFAULT_FILE))

    args = ap.parse_args()
    if args.cmd == "save":
        return cmd_save(args)
    if args.cmd == "restore":
        return cmd_restore(args)
    if args.cmd == "verify":
        return cmd_verify(args)
    if args.cmd == "place":
        return cmd_place(args)
    if args.cmd == "same-desktops":
        return cmd_same_desktops(args)
    return 2


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
